  message: "DONE. Points 1-3 were built in PR #2354, 5 and 6 closed by ruling; points 4 and 7 shipped in PR #2370 (merged 2026-11-24, dev 1acbf00b2).\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, full run of ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/livebook on merged dev (closure/rerun_dev.txt):\n- Point 4, manifest slot: 0 node ids start with manifest: (4 before); the 4 binary nodes sit in swift: (3) and elixir: (1). Fixture demo.cabal: haskell:demo.cabal:5-5:greet:binary.\n- Point 4, template labels: the heex template node's language is on the axis; axis_conformance violations 0 (1 before, that node); 4 heex and 10 eex files are file nodes.\n- Point 7: 56 of 56 js-module package stand-ins have path <external> (WI-hulup closed with its own fixture).\nTWO PREMISES OF THIS ITEM WERE WRONG, found by the build:\n- \"heex for every template\" is not what the linkers did: each labels from its own extension table; seven labels (eex, heex, leex, ftl, vm, jsp, jinja) were off the language axis. They are now LanguageSpec entries with their extensions, as erb / haml / slim are.\n- Neither point moves a stable id (the stable id never hashed the id slot or Symbol.path). The 2026-11-23 ruling's \"only if a bump happens\" was not needed. 51-tree comparison: 59 build-target node ids renamed, 629 package paths changed, 47 template file nodes new, 0 stand-in stable ids moved; edges identical once the renames are applied.\nPUT TO THE OWNER, kept as built: registering the extensions makes those files file nodes everywhere (an Ansible roles tree +301 for .j2). NOT asserted: a tree where a linker renders jinja, ftl, vm or jsp (the Spring linker never activates: filed, tag v20_residual).\n"  # aa97
